---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const steps = [
 ['bdf59cb','Start with the board','Separate hello, display, touch, networking and storage diagnostics made the basic capabilities independently buildable. Lesson: establish the hardware path before designing the full product.'],
 ['5ac04ed','Make a touch application','The calculator moved from board checks to a usable LVGL interface. Connectivity tools followed with scan results and an on-screen keyboard. Lesson: design for a small screen and verify control placement.'],
 ['17a747a','Make it easy to try','GitHub Pages gained a PWA browser flasher and named firmware catalog. Lesson: discovery and installation belong together, with explicit descriptions of what each build does.'],
 ['7b85e91','Connect audio to a local service','LocalLink recorded microphone audio and discovered a LAN speech service. Later microphone diagnostics corrected the input path and added a live meter. Lesson: a successful service request cannot replace checking the actual microphone signal.'],
 ['881fef4','Add appliance behavior','A screen-timeout diagnostic kept touch running while the backlight was off. Speaker, SD file manager and confirmed OTA demos expanded the catalog. Lesson: test each peripheral before combining it with the dashboard.'],
 ['5dd0a64','Bring setup into the browser','BLE provisioning used an on-screen proof-of-possession code. Advertising fixes and separate flash/setup tasks made discovery clearer. Lesson: distinguish provisioning, settings and network health.'],
 ['04b0f27','Build the Codex monitor','A local bridge, animated dashboard and BLE idle settings combined existing capabilities. Mock runs checked quota endpoints, attention and unavailable/recovery states. Lesson: errors and stale state are part of the interface.'],
 ['d5f3fd1','Treat the bridge as a local service','LocalLink management and SSE status streaming reduced manual process handling and made updates more immediate. Quiet mode made the device more practical on a desk. Lesson: network and host lifecycle matter as much as the screen.'],
 ['3dea6f8','Learn local speech first','WakeNet10, MultiNet7 and VADNet were exercised in a visual diagnostic. Frame timing revealed how close command inference could get to the audio deadline. Lesson: measure compute and memory before integrating ML.'],
 ['6bbb88d','Keep an offline recording path','The recorder combined SD, audio and touch with Opus. A codec-stack failure and measured touch latency led to a larger worker stack and independent touch polling. Lesson: host tests help, but device resource constraints need device evidence.'],
 ['9071fcf','Combine speech with the monitor','Local commands and secure monitor Wi-Fi setup required a speech model partition. Device-only allocation failures led to reserving the feed stack and allocating microphone DMA early. Lesson: total free memory does not tell you which allocations will succeed.'],
 ['75155c0','Capture the actual display','LCD readback produced a real screen capture through PlatformIO serial. Lesson: label device captures and host-rendered previews separately.'],
 ['74eb0dc','Clarify the voice interaction','The command guide, microphone feedback, reset bars and explicit quota/agent views refined behavior. Lesson: command listening and message recording need different guidance and timeouts.'],
 ['a24df75','Connect directly to Codex Desktop','An independent USB vendor HID worker added unofficial Codex Micro discovery alongside Wi-Fi. USB microphone support followed, including a Windows audio interface grouping fix. Lesson: enumeration, Desktop discovery, audio capture and button acceptance are separate checks.'],
 ['5a1eac1','Adapt the screen to Desktop controls','A verified Micro session switches the screen from bridge threads to Desktop slots and command keys. Agent colors come from the host; they cannot establish thread names or running counts. Lesson: let verified connection state drive the interface without inventing host semantics.'],
];
---
<Layout title="Build journal"><div class="wrap"><header class="page-head"><p class="eyebrow">Lessons from the commit history</p><h1>Small experiments.<br />A capable appliance.</h1><p class="lede">A high-level trail through the repository, focused on decisions and lessons you can reuse when directing a coding agent.</p></header><div class="prose timeline"><article><h2>2026-10-10 · Bring OTA into the monitor</h2><p>The standalone OTA demo did not make the speech monitor wirelessly updateable: its partition table had one application slot. Monitor 0.7.0 introduces two 4 MiB slots and keeps speech models separate, with a one-time full USB migration. The BLE settings page requests a check or a confirmed installation; the board downloads over verified HTTPS and closes microphone audio during update work. Model hashes and partition identity prevent app-only updates from silently breaking speech, and pending first boots use application rollback. Lesson: carry update compatibility, explicit intent and recovery through the entire product, while keeping hardware evidence separate from compilation.</p><a href="https://github.com/cmwen/FNK0104B/blob/main/docs/monitor-ota.md">Migration, update controls and recovery ↗</a></article><article><h2>2026-10-10 · Publish the guide independently</h2><p>Input fingerprints avoided some compilation, but documentation changes still entered a firmware matrix and waited for its catalog. Guide and browser configuration publishing now use a separate workflow that downloads verified firmware from a successful main build. Firmware and host checks have their own triggers; a new firmware catalog refreshes the guide after it succeeds. Lesson: caching a coupled workflow is different from making its outputs independently publishable. Preserve image provenance, reject partial catalogs, and explain artifact expiry rather than silently recompiling.</p><a href="https://github.com/cmwen/FNK0104B/blob/main/docs/ci-workflows.md">Workflow triggers and recovery ↗</a></article><article><h2>2026-10-10 · Make voice controls explicit</h2><p>The owner reported disappearing USB agent status, an awkward settings layout and microphone gestures that conflicted with Desktop customization. The default now holds the board audio gate open only while Hold to talk is pressed. An optional separate Voice button supports continuous audio, with Desktop assigning the two microphone actions. Mic ON, Mic OFF and Waiting describe outgoing board audio; they do not claim to know whether a desktop voice session ended. The browser separates board preferences from manual Desktop mapping. Lesson: provide useful defaults, explain who owns each setting, and make microphone state observable.</p><p>USB packet loss previously reset the connection epoch and could clear all slots. Fragment recovery now retains the last valid status, while actual disconnects still reset the session. Portable state-machine tests cover voice gestures and settings compatibility; responsive browser checks cover the form. PlatformIO flashing verified image hashes, startup muting and live Desktop status delivery. Voice Chat acceptance and the original dropout still need hands-on testing. Lesson: distinguish a plausible fix, automated coverage and device evidence.</p><a href="https://github.com/cmwen/FNK0104B/blob/main/docs/usb-micro-voice-controls.md">Experience, implementation and remaining checks ↗</a></article><article><h2>2026-10-08 · Rebuild the firmware that changed</h2><p>The guide workflow rebuilt every app even when only documentation changed. Per-environment input fingerprints now track app sources, inherited settings and shared dependencies. Verified cached images keep the full browser catalog available and retain their original build revisions. Missing caches rebuild automatically. Lesson: skipping compilation also requires preserving release completeness and provenance.</p><a href="https://github.com/cmwen/FNK0104B/blob/main/docs/development.md#incremental-firmware-ci--2026-10-08">CI decisions and validation ↗</a></article><article><h2>2026-10-08 · Prioritize configuration and useful USB controls</h2><p>Adding BLE HID shared bonding and a single peer with browser settings. We reserved BLE for configuration and kept USB HID as the computer control path. Repeated Desktop lighting messages were clearing the LCD; unchanged packets now leave it alone, and changed slots repaint individually. Three agent slots plus four joystick controls became the default, with a six-slot setup option. Lesson: preserve configuration access, keep Desktop slot identity stable, and distinguish lighting evidence from running-agent counts.</p><a href="https://github.com/cmwen/FNK0104B/blob/main/docs/usb-micro-controls.md">Decision, implementation and remaining checks ↗</a></article>{steps.map(([sha,title,body]) => <article><h2>{title}</h2><p>{body}</p><a href={`https://github.com/cmwen/FNK0104B/commit/${sha}`}><code>{sha}</code> · inspect the milestone ↗</a></article>)}</div></div></Layout>
